# GLO white keys follow the track. On the song the pad leads, so a key is a chord.
# LFO picks the drone. A drone sitting out is raised while the key is down, then put back.
# PRESETS is a piece. Piece 02's drone is the loud voice, so the key is one note on it.
# ENV is the pad again. SELECT reaches the acid, and knob 2 there is its sound.
# ARP toggles the arpeggiator. It does not change the page.
seed 42
reboot
wait 40
tap GLO
wait 80
expect iam 0
expect view 0
expect piece 2
expect par2 0
key 2 down
wait 40
expect held 4
expect padrel 0x2D
expect litkeys 4
expect par2 0
key 2 up
wait 40
expect held 0
expect litkeys 0
tap LFO
wait 40
expect view 6
key 2 down
wait 40
expect held 1
expect par2 52
key 2 up
wait 40
expect held 0
expect par2 0
turn SELECT -6
wait 40
expect view 0
turn PRESET -1
wait 40
expect piece 1
expect par2 80
expect par0 30
expect par1 45
expect tempo 124
key 2 down
wait 40
expect held 1
expect par2 80
key 2 up
wait 40
expect held 0
expect par2 80
tap ENV
wait 40
expect view 1
key 2 down
wait 40
expect held 4
expect par0 30
key 2 up
wait 40
expect held 0
turn SELECT 8
wait 40
expect view 9
key 2 down
wait 40
expect held 1
expect par1 45
key 2 up
wait 40
expect held 0
expect par40 0
spin K2 1
wait 40
expect par40 1
key 2 down
wait 40
expect held 1
key 2 up
wait 40
expect held 0
expect par40 1
# Two acid keys, one note, through several sixteenths. Letting go leaves nothing held.
tap ARP
wait 40
expect view 9
expect iamarp 1
expect toast ARP
expect toast2 ON
key 2 down
wait 40
expect held 1
key 4 down
wait 40
expect held 1
wait 400
expect held 1
key 4 up
key 2 up
wait 40
expect held 0
tap ARP
wait 40
expect iamarp 0
expect toast ARP
expect toast2 OFF
expect view 9
# A pad chord is four notes. With ARP on it is one, and off again it is the chord.
turn SELECT -8
wait 40
expect view 1
tap ARP
wait 40
expect iamarp 1
expect view 1
key 2 down
wait 40
expect held 1
tap ARP
wait 40
expect iamarp 0
expect held 4
key 2 up
wait 40
expect held 0
